Thank you.

2
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:59,980
Thank you.

3
00:01:00,000 --> 00:01:29,980
Thank you.

4
00:01:30,000 --> 00:01:59,980
Thank you.

5
00:02:00,000 --> 00:02:00,080
Thank you.

6
00:02:00,080 --> 00:02:00,120
Thank you.

7
00:02:01,940 --> 00:02:06,000
Discuss order, converse about order,

8
00:02:06,860 --> 00:02:11,080
and I thought perhaps we could begin with that today,

9
00:02:11,120 --> 00:02:12,080
if that's agreeable with you.

10
00:02:14,580 --> 00:02:19,000
I think we were talking about freedom,

11
00:02:20,960 --> 00:02:24,240
responsibility and relationship.

12
00:02:26,600 --> 00:02:28,600
And before we go any further,

13
00:02:28,760 --> 00:02:29,980
we thought we would...

14
00:02:30,000 --> 00:02:35,000
talk over together this question of order.

15
00:02:35,000 --> 00:02:40,000
What is order in freedom?

16
00:02:44,000 --> 00:02:49,000
As one observes all over the world,

17
00:02:49,000 --> 00:02:53,000
there is such extraordinary disorder.

18
00:02:53,000 --> 00:02:55,000
Oh yes.

19
00:02:55,000 --> 00:02:58,000
Outwardly and inwardly.

20
00:02:58,000 --> 00:03:04,000
One wonders why there is such disorder.

21
00:03:07,000 --> 00:03:11,000
You go to India and you see

22
00:03:11,000 --> 00:03:15,000
the streets filled with people,

23
00:03:15,000 --> 00:03:18,000
bursting with population.

24
00:03:18,000 --> 00:03:23,000
And you see also so many sects,

25
00:03:23,000 --> 00:03:26,000
so many gurus, so many teachers,

26
00:03:26,000 --> 00:03:27,000
so many...

27
00:03:27,000 --> 00:03:28,000
...content.

28
00:03:28,000 --> 00:03:30,000
Contradictory lies.

29
00:03:30,000 --> 00:03:32,000
Such misery.

30
00:03:32,000 --> 00:03:33,000
And you come to Europe,

31
00:03:33,000 --> 00:03:35,000
there is little more order,

32
00:03:35,000 --> 00:03:39,000
but you see when you penetrate the superficial order,

33
00:03:39,000 --> 00:03:42,000
there is equal disorder.

34
00:03:42,000 --> 00:03:44,000
And you come to this country,

35
00:03:44,000 --> 00:03:46,000
and you know what it

36
00:03:46,000 --> 00:03:48,000
is like better than I do,

37
00:03:48,000 --> 00:03:51,000
there is complete disorder.

38
00:03:51,000 --> 00:03:56,000
You may be... drive very carefully,

39
00:03:56,000 --> 00:03:57,000
but go behind...

40
00:03:57,000 --> 00:04:03,000
...the façade of so-called order,

41
00:04:03,000 --> 00:04:07,000
and you see chaos.

42
00:04:07,000 --> 00:04:11,000
Not only in personal relationship,

43
00:04:11,000 --> 00:04:14,000
but sexually, morally,

44
00:04:14,000 --> 00:04:18,000
and there is so much corruption.

45
00:04:18,000 --> 00:04:21,000
All governments are corrupt,

46
00:04:21,000 --> 00:04:24,000
some more, some less.

47
00:04:24,000 --> 00:04:26,000
But this whole phenomenon

48
00:04:26,000 --> 00:04:28,000
of disorder,

49
00:04:28,000 --> 00:04:33,000
how has it come about?

50
00:04:33,000 --> 00:04:39,000
Is it the fault of the religions

51
00:04:39,000 --> 00:04:40,000
that have said,

52
00:04:40,000 --> 00:04:42,000
do this and don't do that?

53
00:04:42,000 --> 00:04:46,000
And now they are revolting against all that.

54
00:04:46,000 --> 00:04:47,000
Yes.

55
00:04:47,000 --> 00:04:52,000
Is it governments are so corrupt

56
00:04:52,000 --> 00:04:55,000
that nobody has any trust

57
00:04:55,000 --> 00:04:58,000
in governments?

58
00:04:58,000 --> 00:05:03,000
Is it there is such corruption in business,

59
00:05:03,000 --> 00:05:06,000
nobody wants to look at it even?

60
00:05:06,000 --> 00:05:08,000
Any intelligent man,

61
00:05:08,000 --> 00:05:10,000
any man who is really serious,

62
00:05:10,000 --> 00:05:13,000
and you look at family life,

63
00:05:13,000 --> 00:05:16,000
there is such disorder.

64
00:05:16,000 --> 00:05:22,000
So, taking the whole phenomena of disorder,

65
00:05:22,000 --> 00:05:25,000
why is there such disorder?

66
00:05:25,000 --> 00:05:28,000
What has brought it about?

67
00:05:28,000 --> 00:05:32,000
Doesn't it appear that there is a sort of

68
00:05:32,000 --> 00:05:36,000
necessary, almost built-in progression

69
00:05:36,000 --> 00:05:40,000
in terms of the way we mentioned necessity earlier?

70
00:05:40,000 --> 00:05:44,000
Once order, so conceived,

71
00:05:44,000 --> 00:05:51,000
is superimposed upon an existing situation,

72
00:05:51,000 --> 00:05:54,000
not only does it not effect

73
00:05:54,000 --> 00:05:56,000
what is hoped for,

74
00:05:56,000 --> 00:05:59,000
but it creates a new situation...

75
00:05:59,000 --> 00:06:00,000
Of course.

76
00:06:00,000 --> 00:06:03,000
...which we think requires a new approach.

77
00:06:03,000 --> 00:06:04,000
Of course.

78
00:06:04,000 --> 00:06:06,000
And the new approach is still the superimposition.

79
00:06:06,000 --> 00:06:09,000
Like the Communists are doing in Russia and China,

80
00:06:09,000 --> 00:06:12,000
they have imposed order,

81
00:06:12,000 --> 00:06:14,000
what they call order,

82
00:06:14,000 --> 00:06:16,000
on a disordered mind.

83
00:06:16,000 --> 00:06:18,000
Yes.

84
00:06:18,000 --> 00:06:21,000
And therefore there is a revolt.

85
00:06:21,000 --> 00:06:23,000
So, looking at all this,

86
00:06:23,000 --> 00:06:25,000
it is very interesting,

87
00:06:25,000 --> 00:06:31,000
looking at all this phenomenon of disorder,

88
00:06:31,000 --> 00:06:36,000
what is order then?

89
00:06:36,000 --> 00:06:40,000
Is order something imposed,

90
00:06:40,000 --> 00:06:42,000
order as in the military,

91
00:06:42,000 --> 00:06:45,000
on the soldier, imposed order,

92
00:06:45,000 --> 00:06:51,000
a discipline which is a conformity,

93
00:06:51,000 --> 00:06:55,000
suppression, imitation,

94
00:06:55,000 --> 00:07:02,000
is order conformity?

95
00:07:04,000 --> 00:07:07,000
Not in the sense if it is artificially imposed, yes.

96
00:07:07,000 --> 00:07:10,000
In any sense.

97
00:07:12,000 --> 00:07:18,000
If I conform to an order,

98
00:07:18,000 --> 00:07:21,000
I am creating disorder.

99
00:07:21,000 --> 00:07:24,000
Yes, yes, I understand what you mean.

100
00:07:24,000 --> 00:07:29,000
In our use of the word conform,

101
00:07:29,000 --> 00:07:34,000
we sometimes mean by it

102
00:07:34,000 --> 00:07:38,000
a natural relation between the nature of a thing

103
00:07:38,000 --> 00:07:41,000
and the activities that are proper to it

104
00:07:41,000 --> 00:07:43,000
or belong to it.

105
00:07:43,000 --> 00:07:46,000
But then that use of the word conform

106
00:07:46,000 --> 00:07:48,000
is not the use that is usual

107
00:07:48,000 --> 00:07:50,000
and the one that we are concerned in here.

108
00:07:50,000 --> 00:07:52,000
No. No.

109
00:07:52,000 --> 00:07:55,000
So, is order conformity?

110
00:07:55,000 --> 00:07:59,000
Is order imitation?

111
00:07:59,000 --> 00:08:04,000
Is order acceptance, obedience?

112
00:08:04,000 --> 00:08:08,000
Or because we have conformed,

113
00:08:08,000 --> 00:08:09,000
because we have obeyed,

114
00:08:09,000 --> 00:08:11,000
because we have accepted,

115
00:08:11,000 --> 00:08:15,000
we have created disorder?

116
00:08:18,000 --> 00:08:20,000
Because discipline,

117
00:08:20,000 --> 00:08:25,000
in the ordinary accepted sense of that word,

118
00:08:25,000 --> 00:08:28,000
is to conform.

119
00:08:28,000 --> 00:08:30,000
Yes, we say in English, don't we,

120
00:08:30,000 --> 00:08:34,000
to someone who appears to be undisciplined

121
00:08:34,000 --> 00:08:37,000
or who in fact is undisciplined,

122
00:08:37,000 --> 00:08:38,000
we say, straighten up.

123
00:08:38,000 --> 00:08:41,000
Straighten up, yes.

124
00:08:41,000 --> 00:08:46,000
The images that we use to refer to that correction

125
00:08:46,000 --> 00:08:48,000
are always rigid, aren't they?

126
00:08:48,000 --> 00:08:49,000
Yes.

127
00:08:49,000 --> 00:08:50,000
Yes, yes.

128
00:08:50,000 --> 00:08:56,000
So that authority,

129
00:08:56,000 --> 00:09:00,000
whether the communist authority of the few

130
00:09:00,000 --> 00:09:03,000
or the authority of the priest

131
00:09:03,000 --> 00:09:05,000
or the authority of someone who says,

132
00:09:05,000 --> 00:09:08,000
I know and you don't know,

133
00:09:08,000 --> 00:09:11,000
that is one of the factors

134
00:09:11,000 --> 00:09:16,000
that has produced disorder.

135
00:09:16,000 --> 00:09:19,000
And one of the factors of this disorder

136
00:09:19,000 --> 00:09:25,000
is our lack of real culture.

137
00:09:25,000 --> 00:09:28,000
We are very sophisticated,

138
00:09:28,000 --> 00:09:31,000
very so-called civilised,

139
00:09:31,000 --> 00:09:32,000
in the sense we are clean,

140
00:09:32,000 --> 00:09:33,000
we have bathrooms,

141
00:09:33,000 --> 00:09:35,000
we have better food and all that,

142
00:09:35,000 --> 00:09:41,000
but inwardly we are not cultured.

143
00:09:41,000 --> 00:09:47,000
We are not healthy, whole human beings.

144
00:09:47,000 --> 00:09:50,000
The inner fragmentation spills out

145
00:09:50,000 --> 00:09:53,000
into our operations externally.

146
00:09:53,000 --> 00:09:59,000
So, unless we understand disorder,

147
00:09:59,000 --> 00:10:00,000
the nature of disorder,

148
00:10:00,000 --> 00:10:02,000
the structure of disorder,

149
00:10:02,000 --> 00:10:08,000
we can never find out what is order.

150
00:10:08,000 --> 00:10:12,000
Out of the understanding of disorder comes order.

151
00:10:12,000 --> 00:10:15,000
Not first seek order

152
00:10:15,000 --> 00:10:17,000
and then impose that order,

153
00:10:17,000 --> 00:10:20,000
and then that order and disorder.

154
00:10:20,000 --> 00:10:21,000
I don't know if I am making myself clear.

155
00:10:21,000 --> 00:10:22,000
Yes, I do.

156
00:10:22,000 --> 00:10:24,000
I am thinking as you are speaking

157
00:10:24,000 --> 00:10:27,000
of the phenomenon

158
00:10:27,000 --> 00:10:30,000
in the world of study

159
00:10:30,000 --> 00:10:33,000
and the world of teaching and learning

160
00:10:33,000 --> 00:10:38,000
as we understand them conventionally.

161
00:10:38,000 --> 00:10:40,000
I have noticed in our conversations

162
00:10:40,000 --> 00:10:42,000
that you always suggest

163
00:10:42,000 --> 00:10:47,000
that we study some dysfunction.

164
00:10:47,000 --> 00:10:50,000
We are never invited really to do that.

165
00:10:50,000 --> 00:10:53,000
We are given the notion

166
00:10:53,000 --> 00:10:56,000
that the thing to study

167
00:10:56,000 --> 00:11:02,000
is the principle involved.

168
00:11:02,000 --> 00:11:04,000
The argument for that, of course,

169
00:11:04,000 --> 00:11:12,000
is that one refers to health

170
00:11:12,000 --> 00:11:14,000
in order to understand disease.

171
00:11:14,000 --> 00:11:16,000
But then the reference to health,

172
00:11:16,000 --> 00:11:17,000
when that is said,

173
00:11:17,000 --> 00:11:22,000
is received purely conceptually.

174
00:11:22,000 --> 00:11:23,000
Quite, quite.

175
00:11:23,000 --> 00:11:25,000
And so what we are studying is now...

176
00:11:25,000 --> 00:11:27,000
Is a concept rather than the actuality,

177
00:11:27,000 --> 00:11:29,000
than the what is.

178
00:11:29,000 --> 00:11:31,000
And we slip out...

179
00:11:31,000 --> 00:11:32,000
Yes, quite.

180
00:11:32,000 --> 00:11:35,000
...of the true task.

181
00:11:35,000 --> 00:11:41,000
There is a difficulty in grasping the suggestion

182
00:11:41,000 --> 00:11:43,000
that we study the disorder...

183
00:11:43,000 --> 00:11:44,000
Disorder.

184
00:11:44,000 --> 00:11:46,000
...simply because disorder

185
00:11:46,000 --> 00:11:48,000
by its own condition

186
00:11:48,000 --> 00:11:50,000
is without an ordering principle.

187
00:11:50,000 --> 00:11:52,000
Quite, quite, quite.

188
00:11:52,000 --> 00:11:54,000
Therefore it sounds, when it comes out,

189
00:11:54,000 --> 00:11:58,000
as though I am being asked to study

190
00:11:58,000 --> 00:12:01,000
something that is unstudiable.

191
00:12:01,000 --> 00:12:03,000
But to the contrary...

192
00:12:03,000 --> 00:12:04,000
On the contrary?

193
00:12:04,000 --> 00:12:05,000
Yes.

194
00:12:05,000 --> 00:12:07,000
Yes, now I will stop.

195
00:12:07,000 --> 00:12:08,000
Go ahead.

196
00:12:08,000 --> 00:12:09,000
On the contrary,

197
00:12:09,000 --> 00:12:10,000
you were about to say something.

198
00:12:10,000 --> 00:12:12,000
On the contrary,

199
00:12:12,000 --> 00:12:15,000
there must be an understanding of disorder.

200
00:12:16,000 --> 00:12:18,000
Why it has come about.

201
00:12:18,000 --> 00:12:20,000
Yes.

202
00:12:23,000 --> 00:12:30,000
One of the factors, sir, is, I think, basically,

203
00:12:30,000 --> 00:12:37,000
that thought is matter,

204
00:12:37,000 --> 00:12:46,000
and thought, by its very nature, is fragmentary.

205
00:12:46,000 --> 00:12:54,000
Thought divides the me and the not me,

206
00:12:54,000 --> 00:12:57,000
we and the my country and your country,

207
00:12:57,000 --> 00:12:59,000
my ideas and your ideas,

208
00:12:59,000 --> 00:13:01,000
my religion and your... and so on.

209
00:13:01,000 --> 00:13:08,000
The very movement of thought is divisive.

210
00:13:08,000 --> 00:13:15,000
Because thought is the response of memory,

211
00:13:15,000 --> 00:13:16,000
the response of thought,

212
00:13:16,000 --> 00:13:20,000
the response of experience, which is the past.

213
00:13:20,000 --> 00:13:25,000
And unless we really go into this question

214
00:13:25,000 --> 00:13:28,000
very, very deeply,

215
00:13:28,000 --> 00:13:31,000
the movement of thought

216
00:13:31,000 --> 00:13:35,000
and the movement of disorder.

217
00:13:35,000 --> 00:13:39,000
That seems to me to be a key word there,

218
00:13:39,000 --> 00:13:42,000
for my understanding, in listening to you,

219
00:13:42,000 --> 00:13:43,000
movement here,

220
00:13:43,000 --> 00:13:45,000
to study the movement of disorder,

221
00:13:45,000 --> 00:13:49,000
would seem to me to take it a step deeper

222
00:13:49,000 --> 00:13:52,000
than the phrase to study disorder.

223
00:13:52,000 --> 00:13:55,000
With the word movement, we are dealing with act.

224
00:13:55,000 --> 00:13:56,000
Movement.

225
00:13:56,000 --> 00:13:57,000
Exactly.

226
00:13:57,000 --> 00:13:59,000
The career of disorder.

227
00:13:59,000 --> 00:14:01,000
Yes.

228
00:14:01,000 --> 00:14:02,000
Yes.

229
00:14:02,000 --> 00:14:07,000
If that is what we are directed upon,

230
00:14:07,000 --> 00:14:12,000
then I think the objection

231
00:14:12,000 --> 00:14:14,000
that the study of disorder,

232
00:14:14,000 --> 00:14:18,000
the study of disorder is to undertake

233
00:14:18,000 --> 00:14:20,000
an impossible pursuit,

234
00:14:20,000 --> 00:14:23,000
is not made with any foundation.

235
00:14:23,000 --> 00:14:25,000
That objection loses its force

236
00:14:25,000 --> 00:14:27,000
precisely at the point when one says,

237
00:14:27,000 --> 00:14:30,000
no, no, it is not disorder as a concept

238
00:14:30,000 --> 00:14:31,000
that we are dealing with here.

239
00:14:31,000 --> 00:14:33,000
It is the movement of it.

240
00:14:33,000 --> 00:14:35,000
It is its own career, it is its passage,

241
00:14:35,000 --> 00:14:38,000
it is the whole corruption of the act as such.

242
00:14:38,000 --> 00:14:40,000
Yes, exactly.

243
00:14:40,000 --> 00:14:41,500
I keep on saying this

244
00:14:41,500 --> 00:14:43,000
business about act all the time,

245
00:14:43,000 --> 00:14:45,000
and perhaps it seems repetitious.

246
00:14:45,000 --> 00:14:47,000
Oh, that is absolutely right.

247
00:14:47,000 --> 00:14:53,000
But, you know, hardly ever is that taken seriously.

248
00:14:53,000 --> 00:14:54,000
I know, sir.

249
00:14:54,000 --> 00:14:56,000
By our species.

250
00:14:56,000 --> 00:14:58,000
Of course, the animals are on to that

251
00:14:58,000 --> 00:15:00,000
from the beginning.

252
00:15:00,000 --> 00:15:01,000
But we don't.

253
00:15:01,000 --> 00:15:02,000
No.

254
00:15:02,000 --> 00:15:05,000
You see that we deal with concepts,

255
00:15:05,000 --> 00:15:10,000
not with what is, actually what is,

256
00:15:10,000 --> 00:15:13,000
rather than discuss formulas,

257
00:15:13,000 --> 00:15:15,000
concepts and ideas,

258
00:15:15,000 --> 00:15:19,000
what is, is disorder.

259
00:15:19,000 --> 00:15:23,000
And that disorder is spreading all over the world.

260
00:15:23,000 --> 00:15:28,000
It is a movement, it is a living disorder.

261
00:15:28,000 --> 00:15:31,000
It isn't disorder which is dead,

262
00:15:31,000 --> 00:15:37,000
it is a living thing, moving, corrupting, destroying.

263
00:15:37,000 --> 00:15:42,000
Yes, exactly. Exactly.

264
00:15:42,000 --> 00:15:43,000
So...

265
00:15:43,000 --> 00:15:45,000
It takes, as you pointed out so often,

266
00:15:45,000 --> 00:15:52,000
it takes an extreme concentration of attention

267
00:15:52,000 --> 00:15:56,000
to follow movement.

268
00:15:56,000 --> 00:16:01,000
And there is a rebellion in us against following movement,

269
00:16:01,000 --> 00:16:08,000
which perhaps lies in our disaffection

270
00:16:08,000 --> 00:16:10,000
with the intuition that we have

271
00:16:10,000 --> 00:16:13,000
that transition is unintelligent.

272
00:16:13,000 --> 00:16:14,000
Quite, quite.

273
00:16:14,000 --> 00:16:15,000
And we don't want that.

274
00:16:15,000 --> 00:16:18,000
We can't stand the thought that there is something

275
00:16:18,000 --> 00:16:21,000
that is unintelligible.

276
00:16:21,000 --> 00:16:25,000
And so we just will not make that active attention.

277
00:16:25,000 --> 00:16:26,000
Quite.

278
00:16:26,000 --> 00:16:27,500
So it is like sitting

279
00:16:27,500 --> 00:16:29,000
on the bank of a river

280
00:16:29,000 --> 00:16:33,000
and watching the waters go by.

281
00:16:33,000 --> 00:16:35,000
You can't alter the water.

282
00:16:35,000 --> 00:16:37,000
You can't change the substance

283
00:16:37,000 --> 00:16:40,000
or the movement of the water.

284
00:16:40,000 --> 00:16:42,000
In the same way this movement of disorder

285
00:16:42,000 --> 00:16:48,000
is part of us and is flowing outside of us.

286
00:16:48,000 --> 00:16:52,000
So one has to look at it.

287
00:16:52,000 --> 00:16:56,000
And there is no confusion in the act at all.

288
